+			'Thanks for the details. Logos come up a lot. Can you tell me two things: how much of the logo is the icon as we drew it, and what {client} plan to do with the logo? In particular, are they planning to register it as a trademark?',
+			'Happy to help. Using library items in client work is covered, but logos have one extra wrinkle, which is trademarks. Do you know whether {client} want to register this logo?'
+		],
+		paths: [
+			// logos and trademarks; allowed as asked
+			{
+				detail: ['I asked. They have no plans to register anything; it’s going on the van, the shop sign, aprons and the website. The icon is maybe a third of the logo and I’ve thickened the lines.', 'No trademark. They’re a {clientKind} with one site; they just want it on their signage, bags and Instagram.'],
+				ends: [
+					[['a', 'Then you’re fine: a logo used on signage, print and online is client work, and the icon can be part of it, changed or not. If they ever decide to register it, come back to us first.'], ['c', 'Perfect, thanks.']],
+					[['a', 'That’s covered. A logo on their van, signs and website is part of your work for them, and they can keep using it for as long as they like.'], ['c', 'Thanks! Out of interest, why does registering make a difference?'], ['a', 'Registering a mark gives the owner the right to stop others using it. The same icon is in the library for every subscriber, so nobody can register it as their own mark. Using it is fine; claiming it as theirs alone isn’t.']]
+				],
+				settled: true
+			},
+			// logos and trademarks; not allowed, offered a custom symbol or a registered wordmark in {font}
+			{
+				detail: ['They do, unfortunately. Their solicitor has said they should register the logo before the launch, and the icon is basically the whole mark. I’ve only changed the colour.\n\nThis is what the solicitor drafted:\n\n{PASTE:tm}', 'Their business partner wants it registered as a trademark in the UK. The icon is the main thing in the logo; the name sits underneath quite small.'],
+				look: ['Logo is mainly the {icon} icon, unchanged apart from colour, and the client wants to register it. Usual answer applies.'],
+				ends: [
+					[['a', 'Thanks for checking first. Registering a trademark means claiming the mark as theirs alone, and the {icon} icon is available to every Pro subscriber, so a mark that is mainly that icon can’t be registered. What other designers do: draw a custom symbol, using the icon only as a sketch, or register a wordmark of the name set in {font}, which is fine because nobody owns a word set in a typeface. The current logo can still be used; it just can’t be registered.'], ['c', 'OK. I’ll redraw the symbol from scratch; it was only a starting point anyway. Thanks.']],
+					[['a', 'In that case the logo as it stands can’t be registered. The {icon} icon is in the library for everyone, so it can’t become one business’s trademark. Two ways round it: a symbol you draw yourself, or a wordmark of the name in {font}.'], ['c', 'Ah. They won’t be pleased, but better now than after launch. If I draw my own symbol and keep {font} for the name, can that be registered?'], ['a', 'Yes. A symbol you drew yourself is yours to pass to them, and the name set in {font} is fine.']]
+				],
+				settled: true
+			},
+			// logos and trademarks; passed to the solicitors
+			{
+				detail: ['They do want to register it, but I’ve changed the icon a lot: different proportions, my own detailing; it’s honestly hard to see where it came from. Their lawyer wants something in writing from you saying it’s OK.', 'They’re registering it. I redrew the icon by hand using yours as a reference, so it’s similar in outline but none of the original paths are left. The client’s solicitor is asking for a letter from Inkwell.'],
+				look: ['Customer wants a written statement for a client’s trademark filing; icon heavily altered. Over to Helen.'],
+				helen: ['I can’t judge “altered enough” from a screenshot, and they want it in writing. Sending the before and after to Calloway Reid.', 'This needs a proper opinion, not a reply from us. Sent to Calloway Reid with both images and the draft filing.'],
+				ends: [
+					[['H', 'Hello {name}, I look after licensing at Inkwell. Because {client}’s solicitor wants a written statement for a trademark filing, I’ve sent your before-and-after images to our solicitors, Calloway Reid. They normally reply within two weeks, and I’ll write to you as soon as I hear.'], ['c', 'Thank you, I’ll let the client know.']],
+					[['H', 'Hello {name}, Helen here; I handle licensing. A written statement for a trademark filing is something our solicitors need to look at, so I’ve sent them the original icon and your version. I’ll be in touch when I have their view.'], ['c', 'Any news from the solicitors? The client is keen to file.'], ['H', 'Not yet, sorry. I chased them on {day} and they’ve promised a reply soon. I’ll write as soon as it arrives.']]
+				]
+			}
+		]
